  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness, specifically the proportion of probability on unfavorable outcomes) is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses on the higher probability of a positive outcome (25% vs. 20%), which is unrelated to the skewness measure. The decision reason’s rule — preferring the more right-skewed lottery (i.e., the one with more weight on the 0 Euro outcome) — is not reflected in the justification. In fact, the individual’s reasoning implicitly favors a less right-skewed lottery (A has 25% chance of 3000, 75% of 0; B has 20% of 4000, 80% of 0), which is less right-skewed than B. Therefore, the individual did not apply the skewness-based decision reason. The reasoning is based on a different criterion (probability of positive outcome), not skewness. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
