  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of the probability mass assigned to unfavorable outcomes (i.e., negative outcomes) to assess skewness and to prefer the more right-skewed lottery (i.e., one with greater probability mass on unfavorable outcomes). In this case, Lottery A has a 0.2% chance of a loss, while Lottery B has only 0.1%. Therefore, A has a greater probability mass on unfavorable outcomes, making it more right-skewed according to the reason. Thus, the reason would prefer A. However, the individual's verbal report does not mention the probability of loss or the skewness of the lotteries. Instead, the individual focuses solely on the high probability of receiving 0 Euros, which is a favorable outcome. The justification is based on outcome certainty, not on the distribution of risk or skewness. Therefore, the individual did not consider the relevant information (probability of unfavorable outcomes) or apply the rule of preferring more right-skewed lotteries. The decision reason was not used. The individual’s reasoning is entirely different and unrelated to skewness or probability mass on negative outcomes. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
